      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1186",
      "html": "<p>Megalonema platycephalum Eigenmann, 1912. Type locality: Tumatumari, Guyana. Maximum size: 300 mm (11.8\") SL, a reasonable guess as the holotype is 126 mm SL. IUCN Red List: Not Evaluated.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1186",
      "html": "<p>Can be offered for sale as Piramutana piramuta, a name currently considered a junior synonym of the much larger B. vailliantii, although these fish look similar when young.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1186",
      "html": "<p>South America: Amazon, Essequibo and Orinoco River basins, including Guyana waters and coastal rivers of the Guianas.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1186",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
